  "problem": "The function $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-x+3, & x<2, \\\\ 2, & x\\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{2}(-x+3)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{2}^{5}2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+3x){|}_{-4}^{2}\\,+\\,2x{|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =[\\,-\\frac{(2)^{2}}{2}+3(2)\\,-\\,(-\\frac{(-4)^{2}}{2}+3(-4))]\\,+\\,[\\,2(5)-2(2)\\,] \\\\  & =[\\,-2+6\\,-\\,(-8-12)]+6 \\\\  & =[4\\,-\\,(-20)]+6 \\\\  & =24+6 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
